{"id":1769663,"retrievedAt":"2026-09-14T17:09:35.678Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":16,"name":"Animation"}],"homepage":"","id":1769663,"imdb_id":"tt0323557","origin_country":["CH"],"original_language":"fr","original_title":"Pam et Poum","overview":"Pam et Poum (1957) is the first animated short film conceived by the Swiss couple Gisèle and Ernest \"Nag\" Ansorge. The project was born entirely in their own apartment, a self-taught endeavor after they discovered the puppetry work of the Czech master Jiří Trnka. The story follows the interactions and small adventures of a stuffed bear and monkey named Pam and Poum. Instead of building an artificial set from scratch, the filmmakers used the furniture, corners, and atmosphere of their own Lausanne apartment as a real-life setting for the figures, bringing the toys to life through frame-by-frame animation. The puppets used originally belonged to Gisèle's nephew.","popularity":0.05,"poster_path":null,"production_companies":[],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"CH","name":"Switzerland"}],"release_date":"1957-06-01","revenue":0,"runtime":10,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"No Language","iso_639_1":"xx","name":"No Language"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Pam and Poum","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"external_ids":{"imdb_id":"tt0323557","wikidata_id":null,"facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"keywords":{"keywords":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"crew":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":1644527,"known_for_department":"Directing","name":"Ernest Ansorge","original_name":"Ernest Ansorge","popularity":0.4766,"profile_path":"/vmr0OUtw407QJW59nSnc0XzKVZ.jpg","credit_id":"6aa691311577829229ecb647","department":"Directing","job":"Director"},{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":1644527,"known_for_department":"Directing","name":"Ernest Ansorge","original_name":"Ernest Anso